      "pageEnd": 44,
      "target": "../sections/page-044.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "32\nDigital implementation investment guide\n3.1.1\t\nDETERMINE THE HEALTH PROGRAMME PROCESSES TO TARGET\nHealth programme processes, also called business \nprocesses, consist of a set of activities or tasks \nperformed together to achieve the objectives of the \nhealth programme area or health system (51). Processes \ninvolve different personas and may cross multiple levels \nof the health system. For example, within the area of \nantenatal care, health programme processes can include \nactivities associated with identifying pregnant women, \ngenerating demand for services, monitoring supplies and \ncommod",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Section 3.1.1 ('Determine the health programme processes to target', page 32) explains how to identify priority business processes and document their objectives, inputs, outputs, task sets, and expected outcomes, illustrated by Figure 3.1.1.1 (a process matrix for an Expanded Programme on Immunization covering Patient management, Vaccination management, Stock management, and Service delivery, cross-referencing Annex 3.1).",
