      "title": "Page 47",
      "pageStart": 47,
      "pageEnd": 47,
      "target": "../sections/page-047.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "35\nIdentify health system challenges and needs\nBID INITIATIVE \nCASE STUDY\nBID Initiative: Business processes\nIt was hard for Oliver Mlemeta, the sister in charge at the Usa River Health Facility in Tanzania, to know how \nmany children to expect on immunization day. To figure out which children were due, she would spend hours \nsifting through dense immunization registries and tallying numbers. Then she had to make sure she had \nadequate supplies on hand. If her vaccine stock was low, she would spend more time calling other clinics and \nretrieving what she needed by motorbike. Sometimes, she wou",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "BID Initiative case study ('BID Initiative: Business processes', page 35) describing immunization day workflows, stock-outs, and manual paper reporting challenges faced by Sister Oliver Mlemeta at Usa River Health Facility in Tanzania, and explaining how the BID Initiative worked with Tanzania and Zambia to define 16 national immunization business processes and link systems including VIMS, RITA Birth Registration, National ID, DHIS2, and the Health Facility Registry.",
