      "pageEnd": 49,
      "target": "../sections/page-049.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "37\nIdentify health system challenges and needs\nFig. 3.2.1. \t Using the 5 Whys model to identify the root cause of bottlenecks.\nSource: iSixSigma: Determine the root cause: 5 whys (54).\nFind more examples and worksheets to support the 5 Whys process in the iSixSigma online library (54).\n3.3 \tPrioritize bottlenecks\nNow that you have a better understanding of their root causes, you can rank the bottlenecks, identifying those \nthat contribute the most to preventing success of the health programme. Although you may ideally like to \naddress every bottleneck, limits on resources often require focusin",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents Figure 3.2.1 (page 37), illustrating the 5 Whys root cause analysis model for a facility medication stock-out (tracing clinic stock-out to under-ordering, unknown demand, lack of monthly historical data, and slow manual aggregation from paper forms), and opens Section 3.3 ('Prioritize bottlenecks') on ranking bottlenecks by resolvability, stakeholder capacity, persona perspectives, and impact.",
