      "narrative": null,
      "content": "43\nCHAPTER \n04\nDETERMINE APPROPRIATE \nDIGITAL HEALTH INTERVENTIONS \nIn the previous chapter, you examined different health programme processes and \nidentified key health system challenges. In this chapter, you will rethink the way \nthese tasks are performed and reflect on interventions to address the identified \nbottlenecks.\nTOOLS\n\t+ Bottleneck-mapping worksheet (Annex 3.2)\n\t+ WHO Classification of digital health interventions (4)\n\t+ Digital health intervention selection matrix (Fig. 4.1.3)\n\t+ Digital Health Atlas (8) or digital landscape review \n\t+ Global Digital Health Index (9) or other dig",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Opening of Chapter 4 ('Determine appropriate digital health interventions', page 43), summarizing the chapter's purpose, tools (Annex 3.2 worksheet, WHO Classification of DHIs, Fig. 4.1.3 selection matrix, Digital Health Atlas, and Global Digital Health Index), objectives, inputs from Chapter 3, and expected outputs (Outputs 4.1 through 4.5 covering prioritized DHIs, enabling-environment assessment, functional/nonfunctional requirements, future-state workflows, and landscape analysis).",
