      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 57",
      "pageStart": 57,
      "pageEnd": 57,
      "target": "../sections/page-057.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "45\nDetermine appropriate digital health interventions\nIn the previous chapter, you examined different health programme processes and identified key health system \nchallenges. In this chapter, you will rethink the way these tasks are performed and reflect on interventions to \naddress the identified bottlenecks (see Fig. 4.1). This is called business process redesign. It is at this stage where \nyou will critically assess whether and how digital health applications may be used to alleviate the identified \nbottlenecks. Then, based on your decision, you can begin to describe what digital health app",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces Chapter 4's focus on Business Process Redesign and Requirements Definition within the CRDM framework in Figure 4.1 (page 45), and distinguishes digital health interventions (discrete functionalities addressing bottlenecks), digital health applications (software and ICT systems executing interventions and health content), and digital health enterprises (applications plus hardware, standards, people, processes, policies, governance, and infrastructure).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
