      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 58",
      "pageStart": 58,
      "pageEnd": 58,
      "target": "../sections/page-058.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "46\nDigital implementation investment guide\nIdentifying and selecting digital health interventions \nincludes the following steps. \n1.\t\nSelect one or more digital health interventions \nto address the prioritized health system \nchallenges (if digital is appropriate). If digital \nis appropriate, select interventions that have \ndemonstrated effectiveness, and determine \nhow these interventions can address your \nhealth system challenges. \n2.\t\nDetermine whether the enabling environment \ncan support the selected digital health \ninterventions. This includes understanding \nthe ecosystem and absorptive c",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Outlines the four steps for identifying and selecting digital health interventions (page 46)—selecting evidence-based DHIs, assessing enabling-environment feasibility, defining requirements and future-state workflows, and leveraging existing enterprise applications—and opens Section 4.1 ('Determine and select digital health interventions for the prioritized health system challenges') introducing the WHO Classification of Digital Health Interventions.",
        "state": "draft",
