      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 61",
      "pageStart": 61,
      "pageEnd": 61,
      "target": "../sections/page-061.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "49\nDetermine appropriate digital health interventions\nFig. 4.1.3. \t Digital health intervention selection matrix.\nSource: Adapted from the WHO Classification of digital health interventions, 2018 (4).\nConsider the range of digital health interventions that \nmay be appropriate for your identified health system \nchallenges. Cross-checking these against the WHO \nevidence-based recommendations and any country \nexperiences will help you identify a set of digital health \ninterventions suitable for the expressed needs. \n2.3\nDecision \nsupport \nfor health \nworkers\n1.1\nTargeted client \ncommunication, \ns",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents Figure 4.1.3 (page 49), the Digital Health Intervention selection matrix mapping UHC coverage layers (Effective, Continuous, and Contact coverage), illustrative programme bottlenecks, and standardized Health System Challenges (HSC 5.3, 5.1, 5.2, and 6.2) to relevant DHIs, distinguishing interventions with a WHO guideline evidence base from other functionally appropriate DHIs.",
        "state": "draft",
