      "id": "library/9789240010567-eng/blocks/prose-page-062",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 62",
      "pageStart": 62,
      "pageEnd": 62,
      "target": "../sections/page-062.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "50\nDigital implementation investment guide\nCASE STUDY\nDetermining appropriateness of digital health interventions \nfor health system challenges \nAs part of the joint process with the Ministry of Health and Sanitation in Sierra Leone for identifying \nhealth system challenges and assessing the appropriateness of digital health interventions, WHO \nconvened stakeholders to review challenges faced within the health system and across different \nprogrammatic areas. This was a consultative process to identify areas of improvement and assess \nwhether digital health interventions may play a role in addr",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Case study and Table 4.1.4 (page 50) from a joint WHO and Sierra Leone Ministry of Health and Sanitation multistakeholder consultation, illustrating how three bottlenecks—inequitable midwife distribution (HSC 2.4), poor medical/power/water infrastructure (HSC 5.2), and frequent drug stockouts (HSC 2.1)—were analyzed by root cause to determine where DHIs (such as DHI 3.1.1, DHI 2.4.4, and DHI 3.2.2) are appropriate versus where nondigital solutions are required.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
