      "id": "library/9789240010567-eng/blocks/prose-page-063",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 63",
      "pageStart": 63,
      "pageEnd": 63,
      "target": "../sections/page-063.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "51\nDetermine appropriate digital health interventions\n4.2\t Determine whether the enabling \nenvironment can support the identified \ndigital health interventions \nDigital health interventions are delivered through digital health applications, which ideally are linked to a \nsupportive digital health platform comprising shared services and enabling components (in cases where \nthere are multiple applications); together with the people, processes and policies that support and use them \nto deliver health services to clients, these applications and platform make up the digital health enterprise. \nSucc",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Section 4.2 ('Determine whether the enabling environment can support the identified digital health interventions', page 51) explains how to assess ecosystem readiness, avoid monolithic 'ball-of-mud' software and technical debt, and review national digital health strategies, investment roadmaps, digital maturity assessments, asset inventories (such as the Digital Health Atlas), and enterprise architecture documentation.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
