        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 65",
      "pageStart": 65,
      "pageEnd": 65,
      "target": "../sections/page-065.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "53\nDetermine appropriate digital health interventions\nDepending on your timeline, you may want to develop \nshort-term plans that take into account the current \nenabling environment, while contemplating medium- \nand long-term plans that benefit from your deliberate \nnew investments to catalyse some components of \nthe environment to mature further. A comprehensive \nanalysis of the enabling environment will also help \nyou document the nonfunctional requirements, \nwhich describe general attributes and features to \nensure usability and overcome technical and physical \nconstraints. Examples of nonfu",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues Section 4.2 (page 53) on aligning short-, medium-, and long-term plans with enabling-environment constraints and deriving nonfunctional requirements (such as offline operation, multilingual interfaces, and password protection), accompanied by Box 4.2.2 cataloging six assessment toolkits (National eHealth Strategy Toolkit, Global Digital Health Index, HIS Stages of Continuous Improvement, HIS Interoperability Maturity Toolkit, Nigeria's enabling-environment assessment, and the ICT for women's and children's health workbook).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789240010567-eng/blocks/prose-page-066",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 66",
      "pageStart": 66,
      "pageEnd": 66,
      "target": "../sections/page-066.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "54\nDigital implementation investment guide\n4.3 \tDetermine what the interventions will need to do\nOnce you have selected which types of digital health interventions will appropriately address your health \nsystem challenges and their suitability for your context, you can start defining the requirements of each \nintervention and the digital health application that will be used to execute the intervention. \nThe requirements should not be just digitizing the \nprocesses identified in the current-state workflows \ndeveloped in Chapter 3; also think through ways that \nintroducing efficiencies can optim",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
