      "target": "../sections/page-084.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "72\nDigital implementation investment guide\nregulation that you will need to examine and determine \nhow to balance. (For more information about regulations \nof medical technologies, see Box 5.2.2.1.)\nAs technology continues to evolve, the procedures and \npolicy considerations for introducing new technologies \nwill also likely need to accelerate. The implementation \nleadership teams may want to consider how new \ntechnologies are integrated into the health system \nand what the policy foundation is for regulating the \ntechnologies. Consider the following questions when \nplanning to meet regulatory",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Concludes Section 5.2.2 (page 72) with key regulatory planning questions and Box 5.2.2.1 (citing the International Medical Device Regulators Forum and WHO medical device regulations), and opens Section 5.3 ('Leadership and governance considerations') and Section 5.3.1 ('Governance') with questions on steering committees, MOUs, cross-departmental coordination between ICT, M&E, and vertical health programmes, and inter-ministerial involvement.",
