      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Section 5.5 ('Services and applications', page 77) provides guidance on leveraging existing hardware and mobile-device management tools, evaluating software licensing and configuration models to avoid vendor lock-in, and conducting four staged testing phases with formal developer sign-offs: continual end-user experience (usability) testing, controlled end-user acceptance testing (UAT), real-life functionality testing, and multi-user load/stress testing.",
