      "pageEnd": 94,
      "target": "../sections/page-094.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "82\nDigital implementation investment guide\nPRINCIPLES FOR \nDIGITAL DEVELOPMENT\nREUSE AND \nIMPROVE1\n\t+ Identify the existing technology tools (local and global), data and frameworks being \nused by your target population, in your geography or in your sector. Evaluate how \nthese could be reused, modified or extended for use in your program.\n\t+ Develop modular, interoperable approaches instead of those that stand alone or are \nattempting to be all-encompassing in their features. Interoperability will ensure that \nyou can adopt and build on components from others and that others can adopt and \nbuil",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarizes the Principles for Digital Development tenet Reuse and Improve, advising implementers to identify and reuse or extend existing local and global technology tools, data, and frameworks, develop modular and interoperable standards-based approaches rather than stand-alone systems, and collaborate through technical working groups and communities of practice.",
