      "target": "../sections/page-095.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "83\nLink the digital health implementation to the enterprise architecture\nOver the course of the previous chapters, you developed a plan for a digital health implementation focused on \naddressing identified health system challenges, with a clear understanding of the digital health interventions \nand other functionalities required. To advance this from being a siloed digital health implementation to an \nexchanged digital health system architecture (see Fig. 1.3.1), it is also important to consider the costs and \nimplementation requirements that would enable you to cohesively benefit from and sup",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Opens the narrative of Chapter 6 on aligning investments with a nationally governed digital health enterprise architecture (referencing ITU’s Digital health platform handbook and OpenHIE), and begins Section 6.1 (Assess the digital health enterprise architecture), explaining how business processes, data, applications, and technology form the functional and technical architectures linked by health data and ICT standards.",
