      "pageEnd": 96,
      "target": "../sections/page-096.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "84\nDigital implementation investment guide\nFig. 6.1.1. \t Digital health architectural approach.\nAlthough this type of architectural vision may not \nexist or be fully developed for your context, you could \nconsult the TOGAF and OpenHIE framework in Fig. 6.3.2 \nto understand the different components typically \nfound in developing a shared digital health enterprise \narchitecture. Understanding the current architecture \nand its constituent functional and technical component \nparts will facilitate understanding the gap between what \ncurrently exists and can be leveraged and what may be \nmissing, re",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues Section 6.1 with Figure 6.1.1 (Digital health architectural approach, depicting the four layers of Business processes, Data, Applications, and Technology) and advises consulting TOGAF and OpenHIE frameworks, conducting systems audits with data-exchange experts, and budgeting for future upgrades, maintenance, and architectural remodelling as programme needs evolve.",
