        "text": "Concludes Section 7.1 by detailing the remaining four implementation phases—Deployment (go-live, pilot end-user testing, and iteration), Integration and Interoperability (continuous review of data-exchange needs as the architecture evolves), Scale (expanding reach, cost per end-user, infrastructure, and staffing), and Sustained Operations (recurring costs, M&E, data use, and informing government budget allocations)—and introduces Section 7.2 (Cost drivers), referencing Table 7.2.1 and the ADB digital health investment costing tool.",
