    {
      "id": "library/9789240010567-eng/blocks/prose-page-121",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 121",
      "pageStart": 121,
      "pageEnd": 121,
      "target": "../sections/page-121.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "109\nMonitor the implementation and use data effectively\nCASE STUDY\nMyanmar “Learning for Impact” model of continuous monitoring\nUNFPA Myanmar developed the Love Question, Life Answer (LQLA) mobile application to promote \naccessibility of evidence-based information about life skills and sexual and reproductive health and rights \nto adolescents and young people in and out of school in Myanmar. Through active promotion on different \nchannels, the number of downloads reached more than 43 000 end-users by the end of 2018. As the app was \nbeing deployed, UNFPA determined that it would not be suffici",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents a case study on UNFPA Myanmar’s \"Learning for Impact\" model of continuous monitoring for the Love Question, Life Answer (LQLA) adolescent sexual and reproductive health mobile application (over 43,000 downloads by end of 2018), including Table 8.2.4 detailing metrics, definitions, and corrective actions across five categories: Stability (system uptime), Fidelity (monthly active end-users), Quality (net promoter score), Health Outputs (SRH and HIV prevention knowledge among youth aged 15–24), and Health Outcomes (uptake of integrated SRH services).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
